; Matomo reads this in addition to config/config.ini.php and never rewrites it,
; which is why the setting lives here rather than being patched into the file
; Matomo owns.
;
; Matomo sits behind nginx, which forwards the visitor's address in X-Real-IP
; and X-Forwarded-For. Matomo ignores those headers unless it is told to trust
; them, so without this every visit is recorded as the Docker bridge gateway
; (172.19.0.0) and no visitor can be located: the country report reads
; "Unknown" for almost everything, and the few entries that do appear are
; derived from something other than the address, so they are not measurements
; of where anyone was.
;
; Only trust these headers behind a proxy that sets them itself. nginx here
; uses $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for and is the only route to the container, whose
; port is bound to 127.0.0.1, so a client cannot forge the header.

[General]
proxy_client_headers[] = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR
proxy_host_headers[] = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_HOST
proxy_uri_header = 1
